# BuildMonitor control plane (required in this repo)

BuildMonitor watches this folder and owns local build / test / watch. **Do not** ask the user to run:

- `dotnet build`
- `dotnet test`
- `dotnet watch run`

unless the control plane is unreachable.

## Handshake (loopback HTTP only — no MCP)

1. Read `%LocalAppData%\BuildMonitor\control-plane.json` when present; else `GET http://127.0.0.1:7700/projects`.
2. Match `projectId` by `rootFolder` to this workspace (case-insensitive path; parent/child OK).
3. Before multi-file edits: `POST /session/busy` with `{ "projectId": "…" }`.
4. After edits: `POST /session/idle` with `{ "projectId": "…" }` (auto-build may run; idle ≠ tests passed).
5. Before claiming build/test success: `POST /run/ship-check` with `{ "projectId": "…", "configuration": "Debug" }` and optional `"filter"`.
6. If `ok` is false, read failures/log and fix — do not claim success.
7. Prefer pause/ship-check over starting a second `dotnet watch` or killing processes.

If the control plane cannot be reached, say so briefly and continue with normal editing; BuildMonitor falls back to its own debounce.
